cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Refusing Committee
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-François
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374
    affiliation: Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Mun Seok
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/sparkainlp-x
abstract: >-
  A heterogeneous committee of holographic membranes at different
  coarse-graining resolutions, each with a Youden-calibrated
  refusal gate; only confident members vote, and unanimous refusal
  is reported as its own outcome. A measured negative result:
  per-member refusal does not fix the plain committee's
  underperformance versus the best single member -- the gate
  filters low-confidence votes while the committee's errors are
  high-confidence, and miscalibrated gates collapse accuracy
  under distribution shift.
keywords:
  - holographic-memory
  - ensemble
  - refusal
  - selective-prediction
  - negative-result
